ClankOS is the operating system for clankas.
This repository holds its container: Debian with GNU Emacs and Org,
in which ClankOS commands run.

A garden is a tree of responsibilities kept in Org files, and the
image's commands tend it: capture, placing, review, sweeping and
sealing, with a start-up and a wrap-up for each session. A garden
declares the methodologies it uses, repositories of skills with
checks, and the image installs them where every session finds them.
"clankos-run help" says what a garden is and lists the commands;
"clankos-run help words" gives each word one line and says where it
is defined; "clankos-run help model" says how the things fit together
and which code enforces each. The same documents are under docs/.

https://www.clankos.org

Each operational skill carries the host launcher and its resources.
Run scripts/build-bundles after changing bin/clankos-run, its installer
or slot helpers, or the runtime command inventory. CI checks the generated
copies with scripts/build-bundles --check. Python 3 is needed to build
bundles; installed launchers use Bash and Docker.
